<p><strong>Item#:</strong> SCP-5921</p>
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Safe</span> Euclid</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5921 is to be contained in a metal cell within Site-53. It shall be placed on a pedestal in the center of the cell with a metal lock only openable with a Head scientist present. The Cell is located on Floor 57 and only authorized personnel is aware of its presence. It is guarded by a minimum of five guards heavily armed who are not aware of SCP-5921.</p>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5921 is a book with the appearance of either a commonly known book or is completely titleless. When SCP-5921 is read It will change the content of the book to match the future of the reader. Subjects have been known to go insane if not allowed to finish the book and often commit suicide. The last chapter of the book always depicts how the Subject will die, even if Subjects are contained and guarded and are physically unable to pass away the way SCP-5921 depicts Subjects will sometimes simply die of a heart-attack or Disappear without a trace. If a specific death location was mentioned in SCP-5921 the Subject will always be found at said location.</p>
<p>SCP-5921 Was classified as a SAFE entity until 1993-05-12 when D-431 broke out of his containment and traveled to Floor 57 dodging all security measures along the way. When D-431 Arrived at Floor 57 he killed three armed guards with his bare hands. When seized by other guards in the vicinity he pleaded to see SCP-5921. D-431 had never been aware of SCP-5921's existence nor had been in contact with someone who had. Upon inspection of SCP-5921, it had started to write about D-431 even though D-431 had never read the book. As SCP-5921's content stated D-431 died of drowning at a nearby dock at 1993-05-21</p>
<p>Upon experiments and research, if no individual has not read SCP-5921 within three days of last use it will start to write about a random person in the vicinity. Therefore SCP-5921 is currently used to execute death row inmates.<br />
<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Other than that SCP-5921 does not pose a threat</span><br />
If another book is present in a 1000 meter area SCP-5921 possesses the ability to switch places with said book. A lot of Staff and Class-D's have started complaining about not being able to read during breaks because of this a new site has begun construction. in the said facility, SCP-5921 will be stored<br />
along with other SAFE SCP's. All Staff in the new site will be aware of SCP-5921's existence and no Class-D's will be stored in the facility.</p>
<p><strong>Addendum:</strong> Multiplication<br />
SCP-5921 has the ability to create another of itself altho the copies do not follow the three-day rule.<br />
SCP-5921 Creates more of itself by instructing the reader to touch SCP-5921 with another book.<br />
instead of transferring the power from one to another, both books keep the power.<br />
this was not until recently when the same effects of SCP-5921 were spotted in another book sitting in a library. SCP-5921-2 Was then transported to Site 53. It is unknown if there exist more copies of SCP-5921 but most scientists believe that there are.</p>

