<p>Hi there, I am not an official critter but let me share some thoughts here.</p>
<p>First off, you must remember that the Foundation is cold, not cruel. Why would they continue testing on the boy when the effects of his anomalous abilities are clear from the beginning? They would hardly go past one or two tests and once they were sure this is a child who happens to return from the dead they would keep him in custody in a somewhat nice cell and call it a day. That's what was done to 053 herself.</p>
<p>If the bulk of your narrative was just testing logs then you don't really have a narrative yet. Few people would be interested in reading about a child being tortured. The narrative needs a progression, an arc, maybe it can be the boy telling his life, or the efforts of a researcher to find the boy's family or what is left of them. The readers must feel something when reading your article, you must define what it is you want them to feel and then write around it. If your goal is to make us feel sorry for the boy I still suggest approaching it on a less gratuitously violent way.</p>
<p>Good luck on your writing!</p>

